e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65427" :question/id #uuid "42a4d9da-f1b0-59e3-b817-4de8af8534c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-65427" :question/problem "What is the exact value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{105}^{∘})?$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-{105}^{∘}={30}^{∘}-{135}^{∘}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x={30}^{∘}$ and $y={135}^{∘},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{105}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}-{135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65427/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65427"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-1708"] :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-274557/field-1/15e9061aa00ad853716397cbd9cd2fdd8070cfac1c90e5ac328f51e9c7876edb" :answer/id #uuid "3b410810-c759-5901-9fdb-3abd6050bc98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274557/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "df3c9c2d-31e4-5e1d-80dd-b627e2b65d06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274557/field-1/15e9061aa00ad853716397cbd9cd2fdd8070cfac1c90e5ac328f51e9c7876edb" :answer-field/choices ["q-274557/field-1/15e9061aa00ad853716397cbd9cd2fdd8070cfac1c90e5ac328f51e9c7876edb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274557" :question/id #uuid "62115611-6812-5fe4-88b8-5e2a1338a624" :question/math-academy-id "q-274557" :question/problem "Using the fact that ${75}^{∘}={135}^{∘}-{60}^{∘},$\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x={135}^{∘}$ and $y={60}^{∘},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({135}^{∘}-{60}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274557/field-1"] :db/ensure [:questi