/id #uuid "e77b626e-16ac-5c05-8607-6ae1d8771abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-141270" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{135}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={135}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{135}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65438"] :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={45}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\